# THIS IS A DISABLE LIST, NOT A WHITELIST.
#
# Modules/makesetup reads Modules/Setup.local first and marks every name it
# finds here as already handled ("first rule wins ... allows users to disable
# modules in Setup.local").  When Modules/Setup.stdlib later defines the same
# module, makesetup skips it and records the name in MODDISABLED_NAMES.  A name
# therefore has to be spelled here to be turned OFF, and must be ABSENT to be
# built.  The list must use the module's own name as Setup.stdlib spells it
# (a bare "ssl" does not match "_ssl").
#
# ssl is disabled for size: wyng-backup transports over ssh via the CP
# command-path rewrite in patches/wyng-backup-0.8.1/0002, not Python TLS.
# TLS-capable paths (urllib.request/http.client) will raise ImportError at
# runtime -- out of scope for the wyng image.
#
# _hashlib must NOT be listed here.  wyng derives its archive key with
# hashlib.scrypt, which hashlib defines only as "from _hashlib import scrypt"
# with no builtin fallback, so without the extension the name does not exist
# and wyng dies with AttributeError as soon as a passphrase is needed.
*disabled*
lzma
curses
dbm
nis
ssl
